49,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,May,,"Looking at the candidates, the Integrated Fare Platform (A) has historical precedent, but the Night Service Extension (D) also had a successful pilot.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,I cannot support (D). The roster books show we have no one left to run it without burning out the staff.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Midori,,"The Crosstown Bus Corridor (B) addresses the mid-city slowness, but (C) Station Access Upgrades might help those connection times.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Shizue,,(A) is blocked by the lack of agreement between operators. (C) is risky because of the pre-war shells.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"(A) would reduce those high contractor fees, but (B) might be easier to fund with the construction balance.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, if (A) and (C) are too risky, and (D) is impossible for staffing, (B) is the logical choice.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I agree. (B) uses roadway crews, and while they are low, it's better than the late-turn crisis of (D).","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Midori,,"I'm torn. (B) helps the mid-city, but (C) uses that spare lift maintenance capacity Benjamin mentioned.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Shizue,,But (C) involves those shells. The voids will stop the work for weeks. (B) is safer.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,(B) aligns with the available capital ledger balance for construction.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,May,,I'll vote for (B). It's a proven need and avoids the pitfalls of the others.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I'm with May. (B) is the most rational choice given the staffing constraints.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Midori,,"If the others are so concerned about the shells and the rosters, I'll concede to (B).","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree. (B) avoids the operator disputes and the underground surprises.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I concur. It's the most fiscally and operationally sound option.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
